1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:03,378
HEY! WE ARE
SO IN LUCK.

2
00:00:03,378 --> 00:00:04,755
TREEGER SAID
WE COULD HAVE

3
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:07,090
ALL THIS COOL STUFF
FROM THE BASEMENT.

4
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:08,467
WAIT RIGHT THERE.

5
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:09,468
OH, NO, NO.

6
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:11,094
I'M PADDLING AWAY.

7
00:00:12,847 --> 00:00:14,097
HUH?

8
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:15,432
WOW. REALLY?

9
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:18,644
WE GOT ALL THIS RUSTY CRAP
FOR FREE?

10
00:00:18,644 --> 00:00:20,020
UH-HUH.

11
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,230
THIS AND A BUNCH
OF BUBBLE WRAP

12
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,274
AND SOME OF IT
IS NOT EVEN POPPED.

13
00:00:26,652 --> 00:00:28,111
( quacking )

14
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:33,868
COULD WE BE
MORE WHITE TRASH?

15
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:46,171
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

16
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:48,173
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

17
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:51,343
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

18
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:55,681
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

19
00:00:55,681 --> 00:00:57,683
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

20
00:00:57,683 --> 00:01:00,644
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

21
00:01:00,644 --> 00:01:04,523
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

22
00:01:04,523 --> 00:01:06,358
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

23
00:01:06,358 --> 00:01:09,486
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

24
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:11,363
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

25
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:14,616
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

26
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:20,288
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

27
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:26,879
HOW DESPERATE AM I?

28
00:01:26,879 --> 00:01:28,296
OH, GOOD THING CHANDLER'S
NOT HERE.

29
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:31,258
HE ALWAYS WINS
AT THIS GAME.

30
00:01:31,258 --> 00:01:33,385
I JUST TOLD MY MOM
I'D CATER A PARTY FOR HER.

31
00:01:33,385 --> 00:01:34,386
HOW COME?

32
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:35,763
BECAUSE I NEED THE MONEY

33
00:01:35,763 --> 00:01:37,138
AND I THOUGHT
IT'D BE A GREAT WAY

34
00:01:37,138 --> 00:01:38,933
TO GET RID
OF THAT LAST LITTLE SMIDGEN

35
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:41,518
OF SELF-RESPECT.

36
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:43,228
I THINK THIS IS A GOOD THING.

37
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:44,855
I DON'T THINK MOM
WOULD HAVE HAVE HIRED YOU

38
00:01:44,855 --> 00:01:47,190
IF SHE DIDN'T THINK YOU WERE
GOOD AT WHAT YOU DO.

39
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:48,609
YOU DON'T HAVE
TO STICK UP FOR HER--

40
00:01:48,609 --> 00:01:51,070
SHE CAN'T HEAR YOU.

41
00:01:53,072 --> 00:01:54,239
HEY...

42
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:55,490
YOU GUYS HAVE ANY JUICE?

43
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:56,575
JUST PICKLE.

44
00:01:58,410 --> 00:01:59,912
HEY, RACH, FUNNY STORY.

45
00:01:59,912 --> 00:02:02,957
I BUMPED INTO JOANNA
ON THE STREET YESTERDAY.

46
00:02:02,957 --> 00:02:04,499
MY BOSS, JOANNA?

47
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:05,960
WOW, THAT MUST HAVE
BEEN AWKWARD.

48
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:08,754
WELL, NO. SHE ASKED ME
IF I WANTED TO GET A DRINK.

49
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:10,547
( nervous laugh )

50
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:13,759
YOU, UH, DIDN'T SAY YES
TO THAT, DID YOU?

51
00:02:13,759 --> 00:02:14,760
NO.

52
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,720
NO.

53
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,305
HELLO, RACHEL.

54
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:24,061
WELL, NOT AT FIRST.

55
00:02:25,353 --> 00:02:27,314
WHAT IS SHE DOING HERE?

56
00:02:27,314 --> 00:02:29,274
( makes bed creaking noises )

57
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:35,196
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.
LAST TIME YOU WENT OUT WITH HER

58
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:36,615
YOU SAID SHE WAS
A BIG, DULL DUD.

59
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:38,158
I JUDGED HER TOO QUICKLY.

60
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,994
THIS TIME WE WERE ABLE
TO TAKE THE RELATIONSHIP

61
00:02:39,994 --> 00:02:42,329
TO THE NEXT LEVEL.

62
00:02:42,329 --> 00:02:45,082
( makes bed creaking noises )

63
00:02:45,082 --> 00:02:47,167
WELL, LAST TIME,
I ALMOST GOT FIRED.

64
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,376
YOU MUST END IT.

65
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,087
YOU MUST END IT NOW.

66
00:02:50,087 --> 00:02:52,006
IT'S NOT LIKE THIS IS
AN EVERYDAY OCCURRENCE FOR ME.

67
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:54,508
USUALLY, I'M PRETTY MUCH
IN THERE BY MYSELF.

68
00:02:54,508 --> 00:02:59,220
( makes bed creaking noises )

69
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:01,015
CHANDLER!

70
00:03:01,015 --> 00:03:03,475
PROMISE ME
YOU WILL END IT.

71
00:03:03,475 --> 00:03:05,435
OKAY. I PROMISE.

72
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:06,603
I'LL END IT.

73
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:08,229
THANK YOU.

74
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,982
I HOPE YOU KNOW
WHAT I'M GIVING UP FOR YOU

75
00:03:09,982 --> 00:03:12,609
BECAUSE SHE'S NOT JUST
THE BOSS IN YOUR OFFICE...

76
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:14,193
IF YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

77
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:16,237
( chuckling ):
YEAH.

78
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,492
OH, SORRY.
I KNEW WHAT HE MEANT.

79
00:03:25,956 --> 00:03:28,291
HOW'S THE
HIRED HELP?

80
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:29,417
DOING GREAT.

81
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:30,669
QUICHES ARE
COMING ALONG.

82
00:03:30,669 --> 00:03:33,672
WHAT'S THIS?
BLUE NAIL POLISH?

83
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:35,716
YEAH. I THOUGHT
IT WAS CUTE.

84
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:37,551
HA! THAT'S WHAT
YOUR GRANDMOTHER'S
HANDS LOOKED LIKE

85
00:03:37,551 --> 00:03:40,054
WHEN WE FOUND HER.

86
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:44,892
LET ME ASK YOU A QUESTION.

87
00:03:44,892 --> 00:03:46,393
WHY DID YOU HIRE ME?

88
00:03:46,393 --> 00:03:47,769
OH, WELL, RICHARD RAVED

89
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:49,437
ABOUT THE FOOD
AT HIS PARTY.

90
00:03:49,437 --> 00:03:51,356
OF COURSE, YOU WERE
SLEEPING WITH HIM.

91
00:03:51,356 --> 00:03:55,069
THEN I HEARD THE FOOD
AT THAT LESBIAN WEDDING
WAS VERY NICE.

92
00:03:55,069 --> 00:03:58,072
I ASSUME YOU
WEREN'T SLEEPING
WITH ANYONE THERE--

93
00:03:58,072 --> 00:04:02,409
THOUGH, AT LEAST
THAT WOULD BE SOMETHING.

94
00:04:02,409 --> 00:04:03,744
OH, MY GOD!

95
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:05,370
DID YOU HEAR THAT?

96
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,664
SHE HIRED ME BECAUSE
SHE THINKS I'M GOOD.

97
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:13,087
OKAY. I DIDN'T HEAR THAT.

98
00:04:13,087 --> 00:04:15,338
OH, YEAH. SHE DIDN'T
HIRE ME OUT OF PITY.

99
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:16,339
IT WASN'T SO SHE
COULD PICK ON ME

100
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:17,632
IN FRONT OF HER FRIENDS.

101
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:19,426
SHE ACTUALLY
THINKS I'M GOOD.

102
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:20,886
WOW!

103
00:04:20,886 --> 00:04:23,388
AND, HEY, IT'S COOL
IF YOU'RE A LESBIAN.

104
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,775
( knock at door )

105
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:39,487
GOOD AFTERNOON.

106
00:04:39,487 --> 00:04:40,530
ARE YOU THE
DECISION-MAKER

107
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,741
OF THE HOUSE?

108
00:04:42,741 --> 00:04:44,076
UH...

109
00:04:48,122 --> 00:04:51,458
DO YOU CURRENTLY OWN
A SET OF ENCYCLOPEDIAS?

110
00:04:51,458 --> 00:04:53,501
NO, NO, BUT TRY THE CLASSIFIEDS.

111
00:04:53,501 --> 00:04:55,587
PEOPLE SELL EVERYTHING IN THERE.

112
00:04:55,587 --> 00:04:57,256
ACTUALLY,
I'M NOT BUYING.

113
00:04:57,256 --> 00:04:58,673
I'M SELLING.

114
00:04:58,673 --> 00:05:00,801
LET ME ASK YOU
ONE QUESTION.

115
00:05:00,801 --> 00:05:04,054
DO YOUR FRIENDS EVER
HAVE A CONVERSATION

116
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:05,680
AND YOU JUST NOD ALONG

117
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,515
EVEN THOUGH YOU'RE
NOT REALLY SURE

118
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:09,184
WHAT THEY'RE
TALKING ABOUT?

119
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:16,024
I'M TELLING YOU,
IT'S TOTALLY UNCONSTITUTIONAL.

120
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:17,025
I TOTALLY AGREE.

121
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:18,318
YEAH.

122
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:22,530
I THINK HE DESERVES
A NOBEL PRIZE.

123
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,199
NO!
NO!
NO!

124
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:26,076
HOW CAN YOU
SAY THAT?

125
00:05:26,076 --> 00:05:29,370
I MEAN, IT WAS LIKE
THE ALGONQUIN KID'S TABLE.

126
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:30,371
( all laughing )

127
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:33,500
( nervous chuckle )

128
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:34,960
EXCUSE ME.
I'M SORRY.

129
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:36,044
YOU HAVEN'T
SAID ANYTHING

130
00:05:36,044 --> 00:05:37,796
FOR ABOUT
2 1/2 MINUTES.

131
00:05:37,796 --> 00:05:40,174
ARE YOU AT ALL
INTERESTED?

132
00:05:40,174 --> 00:05:41,925
YEAH, YEAH. YEAH, OH, YEAH.

133
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:43,135
COME ON IN.
OKAY.

134
00:05:46,805 --> 00:05:48,015
THAT'S WEIRD.

135
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:49,683
WHAT?
YOUR NAILS.

136
00:05:49,683 --> 00:05:51,350
I NEVER WEAR FAKE ONES.

137
00:05:51,350 --> 00:05:52,686
I JUST DID IT SO MY MOM
WOULDN'T GIVE ME GRIEF

138
00:05:52,686 --> 00:05:53,937
ABOUT BITING THEM.

139
00:05:53,937 --> 00:05:55,522
OH. NO, I MEANT
IT'S WEIRD

140
00:05:55,522 --> 00:05:57,858
THAT YOU ONLY
HAVE NINE NOW.

141
00:06:00,527 --> 00:06:03,280
OH, MY GOD.

142
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,948
WAIT A MINUTE.

143
00:06:04,948 --> 00:06:06,783
I HAD THEM WHEN I PUT...

144
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:08,535
OH, MY GOD,
IT'S IN THE QUICHE!

145
00:06:09,703 --> 00:06:10,704
OH, MY GOD!

146
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:12,206
OKAY, DON'T PANIC.

147
00:06:12,206 --> 00:06:14,415
I'M GOING TO GET YOU
ANOTHER SET OF NAILS.

148
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:16,168
NO ONE'S GOING TO KNOW,
AND YOU'RE GOING TO LOOK GREAT.

149
00:06:18,253 --> 00:06:21,131
OH. OH, IT'S 'CAUSE
THEY'RE GOING TO EAT.

150
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:22,465
THAT'S THE PROBLEM.

151
00:06:23,925 --> 00:06:25,969
HONEY, DON'T BITE
YOUR NAILS.

152
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:32,351
OKAY, UH, PLEASE DON'T
FREAK OUT, UM, BUT, UH...

153
00:06:32,351 --> 00:06:35,312
THERE'S A BLUE FINGERNAIL
IN-IN ONE OF THE QUICHE CUPS

154
00:06:35,312 --> 00:06:37,731
AND THERE'S NO WAY
TO KNOW WHICH ONE.

155
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:44,738
AND WHOEVER FINDS IT
WINS THE PRIZE.

156
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:46,365
I'M NOT FREAKING OUT.

157
00:06:46,365 --> 00:06:47,949
WHY ARE YOU LAUGHING?

158
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:51,245
IT'S JUST THAT NOW
YOUR FATHER OWES ME $5.

159
00:06:51,245 --> 00:06:52,453
WHAT? YOU BET
I'D LOSE A NAIL?

160
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:54,039
OH, NO. DON'T BE SILLY.

161
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:56,333
I JUST BET THAT
I'D NEED THESE.

162
00:06:56,333 --> 00:06:59,836
FROZEN LASAGNAS?

163
00:06:59,836 --> 00:07:02,421
YOU BET THAT I'D SCREW UP?

164
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:03,840
SO ALL THAT STUFF
ABOUT HIRING ME

165
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,008
BECAUSE I WAS GOOD WAS...

166
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:06,676
NO. THAT WAS ALL TRUE.

167
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:10,013
THIS WAS JUST IN CASE
YOU PULLED A MONICA.

168
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:13,641
YOU PROMISED DR. WEINBERG
YOU'D NEVER USE THAT PHRASE.

169
00:07:13,641 --> 00:07:16,436
OH, HONEY, COME ON.
HAVE A SENSE OF HUMOR.

170
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,521
YOU'RE NEVER ABLE
TO LAUGH AT YOURSELF.

171
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:19,480
THAT'S RIGHT.

172
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:20,732
( chuckles )

173
00:07:20,732 --> 00:07:22,734
MY MOM DOESN'T HAVE
ANY FAITH IN ME.

174
00:07:22,734 --> 00:07:23,860
THAT'S HILARIOUS!

175
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:26,029
( forced laugh )

176
00:07:26,029 --> 00:07:29,116
I DON'T GET IT.

177
00:07:29,116 --> 00:07:31,034
NO, I HAVE FAITH.

178
00:07:31,034 --> 00:07:32,869
NO, YOU HAVE LASAGNAS.

179
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:39,876
( bell rings )

180
00:07:39,876 --> 00:07:42,170
OH, THE RUINED QUICHES
ARE READY.

181
00:07:51,263 --> 00:07:55,058
IT JUST DOESN'T FEEL
LIKE WE'RE BREAKING UP.

182
00:07:55,058 --> 00:07:56,643
NO, WE ARE.

183
00:07:56,643 --> 00:07:58,979
I'M SAD.

184
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:01,315
OKAY.

185
00:08:01,315 --> 00:08:03,691
( phone rings )

186
00:08:03,691 --> 00:08:05,777
YES?

187
00:08:05,777 --> 00:08:07,612
CAN YOU WAIT
TILL TOMORROW?

188
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:10,031
ALL RIGHT.

189
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:12,491
UNBELIEVABLE!

190
00:08:12,491 --> 00:08:13,785
THANKS.

191
00:08:15,287 --> 00:08:16,288
NO. THAT WAS MY BOSS.

192
00:08:16,288 --> 00:08:17,289
I HAVE TO GO.

193
00:08:17,289 --> 00:08:19,040
OKAY.

194
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,375
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

195
00:08:20,375 --> 00:08:21,542
I'M GETTING DRESSED.

196
00:08:21,542 --> 00:08:22,669
WHY?

197
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:24,338
WHEN I WALK OUTSIDE NAKED

198
00:08:24,338 --> 00:08:27,007
PEOPLE THROW GARBAGE AT ME.

199
00:08:27,007 --> 00:08:28,675
WAIT.

200
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:30,469
I WANT TO SHOW YOU SOMETHING.

201
00:08:30,469 --> 00:08:31,886
WHAT IS IT?

202
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:34,889
JUST A LITTLE GAG GIFT
SOMEBODY GAVE ME.

203
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:35,890
PUT YOUR HANDS
TOGETHER.

204
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:38,226
( chuckles )

205
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:39,686
YOU'RE NOT THE BOSS OF ME.

206
00:08:42,189 --> 00:08:43,482
YEAH, YOU ARE.

207
00:08:45,192 --> 00:08:46,901
HMM...

208
00:08:46,901 --> 00:08:48,195
SAUCY.

209
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:57,287
I'LL BE BACK
IN TWO MINUTES.

210
00:08:57,287 --> 00:08:59,414
YOU'RE, UH... YOU'RE GOING
TO LEAVE ME LIKE THIS?

211
00:08:59,414 --> 00:09:01,708
KNOWING YOU'RE HERE,
WAITING FOR ME

212
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:03,668
I THINK THAT'S KIND OF EXCITING,
DON'T YOU?

213
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:07,297
OKAY, BUT IF YOU DON'T
COME BACK SOON...

214
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:10,008
THERE'S PRETTY MUCH NOTHING
I CAN DO ABOUT IT.

215
00:09:12,135 --> 00:09:13,470
OH, HI.

216
00:09:13,470 --> 00:09:15,555
HI. I BROUGHT YOU BACK
A MACAROON.

217
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:18,641
GREAT. I'LL KEEP IT IN MY BUTT
WITH YOUR NOSE.

218
00:09:26,149 --> 00:09:27,608
THAT'S WEIRD.
SHE LOCKED THE DOOR.

219
00:09:27,608 --> 00:09:29,194
YOU KNOW WHY?

220
00:09:29,194 --> 00:09:31,279
SHE'S GOT THE CHRISTMAS
BONUS LIST IN THERE.

221
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:32,989
I SAW HER WORKING ON IT
THIS MORNING.

222
00:09:32,989 --> 00:09:37,077
OKAY. SWEAR YOU WON'T TELL,
BUT WHEN MARK LEFT

223
00:09:37,077 --> 00:09:38,703
HE GAVE ME A KEY
TO JOANNA'S OFFICE.

224
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:39,954
YOU WANT TO SEE THE LIST?

225
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,664
YEAH!

226
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:46,169
( both gasp )

227
00:09:51,466 --> 00:09:52,926
HI.

228
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,263
HOW ARE YOU?

229
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,315
( phone ringing )

230
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,820
( ringing continues )

231
00:10:18,910 --> 00:10:20,537
HELLO. JOANNA...

232
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:25,917
...'S OFFICE.

233
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:28,795
Joanna:
It's me. I'm really,
really sorry

234
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:30,380
but I may be
a little while longer.

235
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,631
HOW LITTLE?

236
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:33,341
A couple of hours.
I feel awful.

237
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:34,342
THIS ISN'T FUNNY.

238
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:35,843
GET BACK HERE RIGHT NOW.

239
00:10:35,843 --> 00:10:36,928
I can't.
WHY NOT?

240
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:39,097
I'm in my boss's car.

241
00:10:39,097 --> 00:10:41,641
WHAT?!
Uh-oh. Tunnel.

242
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:52,235
( intercom buzzes )

243
00:10:54,946 --> 00:10:56,739
( buzzing )

244
00:10:58,116 --> 00:10:59,784
WHAT?

245
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:02,745
Chandler:
Rachel, could I see you
for a moment?

246
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:12,755
OKAY, HERE'S THE SITUATION--

247
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:15,300
THE KEYS TO THE CUFFS
ARE ON THE BACK OF THE DOOR.

248
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,177
COULD YOU BE A DOLL
AND GRAB THEM

249
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:19,220
AND SCOOT ON OVER HERE
AND UNLOCK ME?

250
00:11:21,598 --> 00:11:23,308
AND, ON A TOTALLY
SEPARATE SUBJECT

251
00:11:23,308 --> 00:11:24,892
THAT IS A LOVELY PANTSUIT.

252
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:30,357
YOU PROMISED
YOU WOULD BREAK UP WITH HER.

253
00:11:30,357 --> 00:11:31,690
I DID BREAK UP WITH HER.

254
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:36,695
SHE JUST TOOK IT
REALLY, REALLY WELL.

255
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:39,324
AND THE FACT THAT YOU WERE
JEOPARDIZING MY CAREER

256
00:11:39,324 --> 00:11:40,825
NEVER ENTERED YOUR MIND?

257
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:42,410
IT DID ENTER MY MIND

258
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:44,787
BUT THEN SOMETHING
HAPPENED THAT MADE IT

259
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:47,666
SHOOT RIGHT OUT.

260
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:48,916
YOU KNOW WHAT, CHANDLER?

261
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:50,627
YOU GOT YOURSELF
INTO THOSE CUFFS

262
00:11:50,627 --> 00:11:52,295
YOU GET YOURSELF OUT OF THEM.

263
00:11:52,295 --> 00:11:53,712
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

264
00:11:53,712 --> 00:11:55,632
I CAN'T GET MYSELF
RIGHT OUT OF THEM.

265
00:11:55,632 --> 00:11:56,757
YOU MUST HAVE ME CONFUSED

266
00:11:56,757 --> 00:12:00,094
WITH THE
AMAZING CHANDLER.

267
00:12:00,094 --> 00:12:01,804
COME ON! YOU HAVE TO UNLOCK ME.

268
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:04,432
SHE COULD BE GONE FOR HOURS
AND I'M COLD AND...

269
00:12:06,893 --> 00:12:08,228
OH, CHANDLER!

270
00:12:08,228 --> 00:12:09,979
ALL RIGHT. THIS IS IT.

271
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:11,565
YOU NEVER SEE JOANNA AGAIN.

272
00:12:11,565 --> 00:12:12,982
NEVER.

273
00:12:12,982 --> 00:12:14,651
YOU NEVER COME
INTO THIS OFFICE AGAIN.

274
00:12:14,651 --> 00:12:16,319
FINE.

275
00:12:16,319 --> 00:12:17,736
YOU GIVE ME BACK MY WALKMAN.

276
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:19,738
I...

277
00:12:19,738 --> 00:12:23,451
I NEVER BORROWED YOUR WALKMAN.

278
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:24,994
WELL, THEN I LOST IT.
YOU BUY ME ONE.

279
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:26,663
YOU GOT IT.
HERE WE GO.

280
00:12:26,663 --> 00:12:28,415
COME ON.
THIS IS GREAT.

281
00:12:29,832 --> 00:12:31,376
AH...!

282
00:12:31,376 --> 00:12:33,169
DOES IT HURT?

283
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:34,837
NO. I JUST ALWAYS
SEE GUYS DOING THIS

284
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:36,964
WHEN THEY GET HANDCUFFS
TAKEN OFF THEM.

285
00:12:39,175 --> 00:12:40,801
HELLO, SWEET PANTS.

286
00:12:42,262 --> 00:12:44,013
WAIT A MINUTE.

287
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:46,266
WHAT ARE YOU GOING
TO TELL JOANNA?
ABOUT WHAT?

288
00:12:46,266 --> 00:12:48,851
WHEN SHE SEES YOU'RE GONE,
SHE'LL KNOW I LET YOU OUT

289
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:51,104
AND I WAS IN HERE
AND I'LL GET FIRED.

290
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:53,356
I'LL MAKE SOMETHING UP.
I'M GOOD AT LYING.

291
00:12:53,356 --> 00:12:55,233
I ACTUALLY DID
BORROW YOUR WALKMAN.

292
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:57,235
THERE'S NOTHING
TO MAKE UP.

293
00:12:57,235 --> 00:12:58,777
SHE'S GOING TO KNOW I HAVE
A KEY TO HER OFFICE.

294
00:12:58,777 --> 00:13:00,821
I'VE GOT TO GET YOU LOCKED
BACK THE WAY YOU WERE.

295
00:13:00,821 --> 00:13:04,075
OH, I DON'T THINK SO.

296
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:06,077
NAH, NAH, NAH,
NAH, NO...

297
00:13:06,077 --> 00:13:07,287
NO, NO, NO!

298
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:08,455
NO!

299
00:13:08,455 --> 00:13:09,414
NO!

300
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,874
( shrieks )

301
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:16,337
WELL, THIS IS
MUCH BETTER.

302
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:22,009
SO, HERE'S SOMEBODY
INTERESTING, JOEY.

303
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:24,554
WHAT DO YOU KNOW
ABOUT VAN GOGH?

304
00:13:24,554 --> 00:13:26,556
UH... HE CUT OFF HIS EAR.

305
00:13:26,556 --> 00:13:27,974
AND?

306
00:13:27,974 --> 00:13:29,892
I'M OUT.

307
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:31,436
HE PAINTED THAT.

308
00:13:31,436 --> 00:13:34,731
WOW, THAT'S PRETTY NICE.

309
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:37,776
I THOUGHT HE CUT OFF
HIS EAR 'CAUSE HE SUCKED.

310
00:13:37,776 --> 00:13:38,943
WHAT ELSE
YOU GOT IN THERE?

311
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:41,362
LET'S SEE. UH...

312
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:42,697
WHERE DOES
THE POPE LIVE?

313
00:13:42,697 --> 00:13:45,074
IN THE WOODS.

314
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:48,202
NO, WAIT. WAIT.
THAT'S THE JOKE ANSWER.

315
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:50,871
ACTUALLY,
IT'S VATICAN CITY.

316
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:52,290
NOW, UH...

317
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:55,126
WHAT DO YOU KNOW
ABOUT VULCANIZED RUBBER?

318
00:13:55,126 --> 00:13:59,130
SPOCK'S BIRTH CONTROL.

319
00:13:59,130 --> 00:14:01,007
YOU NEED THESE BOOKS.

320
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:06,220
( knock at door )

321
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,347
HEY.

322
00:14:07,347 --> 00:14:08,847
HI.

323
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:11,058
THIS USED
TO BE YOUR ROOM?

324
00:14:11,058 --> 00:14:12,686
WOW, YOU MUST
HAVE BEEN

325
00:14:12,686 --> 00:14:16,773
IN REALLY GOOD
SHAPE AS A KID.

326
00:14:16,773 --> 00:14:19,693
OH, I'M SUCH AN IDIOT.

327
00:14:19,693 --> 00:14:22,862
I CAN'T BELIEVE I ACTUALLY
THOUGHT SHE COULD CHANGE.

328
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:25,865
LOOK, WHO CARES WHAT
YOUR MOM THINKS?

329
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:28,785
SO YOU PULLED
A MONICA.

330
00:14:28,785 --> 00:14:31,705
OH, GOOD.
I'M GLAD THAT'S CATCHING ON.

331
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:33,665
WHY DOES THAT HAVE
TO BE A BAD THING?

332
00:14:33,665 --> 00:14:35,249
JUST CHANGE WHAT IT MEANS.

333
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:37,669
GO DOWN THERE
AND PROVE YOUR MOTHER WRONG.

334
00:14:37,669 --> 00:14:39,504
YOU FINISH THE JOB
YOU WERE HIRED TO DO.

335
00:14:39,504 --> 00:14:42,215
WE'LL CALL THAT
"PULLING A MONICA."

336
00:14:42,215 --> 00:14:43,717
WHAT?

337
00:14:43,717 --> 00:14:46,594
OKAY, UM... IF A KID
GETS STRAIGHT A's

338
00:14:46,594 --> 00:14:48,847
HIS PARENTS WOULD SAY,
"YEAH! YOU PULLED A MONICA."

339
00:14:50,849 --> 00:14:52,975
OR A FIREMAN SAVES A BABY,
AND THEY GO, "YEAH, I KNOW.

340
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:55,978
HE PULLED
A MONICA."

341
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:57,647
OR SOMEONE HITS A HOME RUN

342
00:14:57,647 --> 00:15:00,567
AND THE ANNOUNCER SAYS,
"YEAH, THAT ONE'S OUT OF HERE."

343
00:15:00,567 --> 00:15:04,153
'CAUSE SOME THINGS DON'T CHANGE.

344
00:15:04,153 --> 00:15:06,781
ALL RIGHT. I'LL GO DOWN THERE

345
00:15:06,781 --> 00:15:08,533
BUT I'M NOT GOING
TO SERVE THE LASAGNA.

346
00:15:08,533 --> 00:15:10,869
I'M GOING TO SERVE
SOMETHING THAT I MAKE.

347
00:15:10,869 --> 00:15:14,831
WAIT.

348
00:15:14,831 --> 00:15:16,457
OOH.

349
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:19,085
OH, WOW!

350
00:15:19,085 --> 00:15:21,212
OH, MY BREASTS
ARE REALLY STRONG.

351
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:27,594
( grunting )

352
00:15:27,594 --> 00:15:29,303
OH, CHANDLER...
CHANDLER, PLEASE.

353
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,389
I HAVE TO GET YOU LOCKED UP
BACK THE WAY YOU WERE.

354
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:33,892
I AM SO GOING TO LOSE MY JOB.

355
00:15:33,892 --> 00:15:37,144
SHE'S VERY PRIVATE
ABOUT HER OFFICE.

356
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:39,355
NOW I KNOW WHY.

357
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:41,399
LOOK, YOU WERE
IN TROUBLE EITHER WAY.

358
00:15:41,399 --> 00:15:43,902
IF SHE SEES ME LOCKED TO THIS
INSTEAD OF THE CHAIR

359
00:15:43,902 --> 00:15:44,985
SHE'LL KNOW YOU WERE IN HERE.

360
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:46,028
SO YOU MIGHT AS WELL

361
00:15:46,028 --> 00:15:50,032
JUST LET ME GO.

362
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:51,492
WHAT IF I CLEAN YOUR BATHROOM
FOR A MONTH?

363
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:54,370
IT STILL
WOULDN'T BE CLEAN.

364
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:58,207
ALL I WANT IS MY FREEDOM.

365
00:15:58,207 --> 00:16:00,334
FOOT RUBS FOR A MONTH.
FREEDOM!

366
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:02,420
I'LL TAKE ALL OF YOUR PHOTOS
AND I'LL PUT THEM INTO ALBUMS.

367
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,088
FREEDOM! I WANT MY FREEDOM!

368
00:16:04,088 --> 00:16:05,423
WHY WON'T
YOU HEAR ME?

369
00:16:05,423 --> 00:16:06,925
SOPHIE,
HELP ME!
HELP ME!

370
00:16:06,925 --> 00:16:08,426
SOPHIE, SIT!

371
00:16:08,426 --> 00:16:09,469
FREEDOM!

372
00:16:09,469 --> 00:16:10,969
( muffled yelling )

373
00:16:10,969 --> 00:16:12,388
WILL YOU
JUST CALM DOWN?

374
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:13,681
( muffled
yelling )

375
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:22,982
I'M GOING TO SAY THIS
FOR THE LAST TIME.

376
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:25,234
WOULD YOU PLEASE JUST...?

377
00:16:29,988 --> 00:16:33,117
WELL, THERE'S A LOT
I DIDN'T KNOW ABOUT VOMIT.

378
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:36,120
( quacking )

379
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:39,707
IN A MINUTE.

380
00:16:39,707 --> 00:16:41,167
SO, WHAT DO YOU SAY, JOEY?

381
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:45,003
YOU GET THE WHOLE SET
OF ENCYCLOPEDIAS FOR $1,200.

382
00:16:45,003 --> 00:16:47,924
THAT WORKS OUT
TO JUST 50 BUCKS A BOOK.

383
00:16:47,924 --> 00:16:49,550
$1,200?

384
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:54,430
YOU THINK I HAVE $1,200?

385
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:56,390
I'M HOME IN THE MIDDLE
OF THE DAY

386
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,476
AND I GOT PATIO FURNITURE
IN MY LIVING ROOM.

387
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:01,771
I GUESS
THERE'S A FEW THINGS

388
00:17:01,771 --> 00:17:04,440
YOU DON'T GET
FROM BOOK LEARNING.

389
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:07,109
WELL, UH... WHAT CAN YOU SWING?

390
00:17:07,109 --> 00:17:08,695
HOW ABOUT ZERO DOWN

391
00:17:08,695 --> 00:17:12,156
AND ZERO A MONTH
FOR A LONG, LONG TIME?

392
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:14,909
YOU DON'T HAVE... ANYTHING?

393
00:17:14,909 --> 00:17:17,411
YOU WANT
TO SEE WHAT I GOT?

394
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:19,038
OKAY. I GOT...

395
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:21,081
A BABY TOOTSIE ROLL

396
00:17:21,081 --> 00:17:23,918
A MOVIE STUB,
KEYS, A KLEENEX...

397
00:17:26,337 --> 00:17:27,797
A ROCK...

398
00:17:27,797 --> 00:17:30,132
AND AN ARMY MAN. MAN!

399
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:32,301
OKAY, I...
I GET THE PICTURE.

400
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:34,387
UH... THANKS
FOR YOUR TIME.

401
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:36,014
AND A 50.

402
00:17:36,014 --> 00:17:37,431
HUH.

403
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:39,600
THESE MUST BE CHANDLER'S PANTS.

404
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:42,520
FOR 50 BUCKS,
YOU CAN GET ONE BOOK.

405
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:45,732
WHAT WILL IT BE--
"A," "B," "C"?

406
00:17:45,732 --> 00:17:47,525
I THINK I'M GOING
TO STICK WITH THE "V."

407
00:17:47,525 --> 00:17:49,610
I WANT TO SEE
HOW THIS BAD BOY TURNS OUT.

408
00:17:54,072 --> 00:17:55,449
Rachel:
I, UH...

409
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:57,493
WILL BUY AND WRAP
ALL OF YOUR CHRISTMAS GIFTS.

410
00:17:57,493 --> 00:17:59,245
NO!

411
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:03,249
I, UH... I'LL SQUEEZE YOU FRESH
ORANGE JUICE EVERY MORNING.

412
00:18:03,249 --> 00:18:04,333
WITH EXTRA PULP?
YEAH!

413
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,334
NO!

414
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:06,627
( grunts )

415
00:18:08,963 --> 00:18:11,716
I'VE GOT IT.

416
00:18:11,716 --> 00:18:14,052
YOU DON'T HAVE IT.

417
00:18:14,052 --> 00:18:16,512
I HAVE SO GOT IT.

418
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,305
THERE'S GOING
TO BE RUMORS ABOUT THIS.

419
00:18:18,305 --> 00:18:19,599
THERE'S NO WAY TO STOP IT.

420
00:18:19,599 --> 00:18:21,601
SOPHIE KNOWS.
MONICA AND PHOEBE KNOW.

421
00:18:21,601 --> 00:18:22,977
HOW COME MONICA
AND PHOEBE KNOW?

422
00:18:22,977 --> 00:18:25,438
OH, I CALLED THEM.

423
00:18:25,438 --> 00:18:27,774
AND WHEN THEY ASK ME WHAT I SAW

424
00:18:27,774 --> 00:18:30,777
I CAN BE VERY GENEROUS...

425
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:34,614
OR VERY STINGY.

426
00:18:37,033 --> 00:18:38,826
GO ON.

427
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:41,120
I CAN MAKE YOU A LEGEND.

428
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:45,917
I CAN MAKE YOU
THIS GENERATION'S MILTON BERLE.

429
00:18:45,917 --> 00:18:46,918
AND MILTON BERLE HAS...?

430
00:18:46,918 --> 00:18:49,378
AW, NOT COMPARED TO YOU.

431
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:56,135
WELL, THEY'RE NOT EVEN
TOUCHING THE LASAGNA.

432
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:57,678
REALLY?
THEY LOVE
YOUR CASSEROLE.

433
00:18:57,678 --> 00:18:59,305
YES!

434
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:00,848
IT'S HARD TO BELIEVE
JUST A LITTLE WHILE AGO

435
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:03,810
THIS WAS NOTHING
BUT INGREDIENTS.

436
00:19:05,478 --> 00:19:08,481
EVERYONE SEEMS
TO LIKE YOUR DISH.

437
00:19:08,481 --> 00:19:10,149
AND YOU?

438
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:13,193
I THOUGHT IT WAS...

439
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:15,905
QUITE TASTY.

440
00:19:15,905 --> 00:19:17,073
SO IF EVERYONE LIKED IT

441
00:19:17,073 --> 00:19:18,992
AND YOU LIKED IT

442
00:19:18,992 --> 00:19:21,201
THAT WOULD
MAKE THIS A SUCCESS.

443
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:22,369
WHICH WOULD MAKE YOU...

444
00:19:22,369 --> 00:19:25,164
A BITCH?

445
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:26,373
WELL, I WAS GOING
FOR "WRONG"

446
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:29,627
BUT WE CAN USE YOUR WORD.

447
00:19:29,627 --> 00:19:32,254
YES, WELL, I WAS WRONG

448
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:33,714
AND I HAVE TO SAY...

449
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:39,012
YOU REALLY
IMPRESSED ME TODAY.

450
00:19:39,012 --> 00:19:40,346
WOW.

451
00:19:40,346 --> 00:19:43,891
YOU MIGHT EVEN SAY
THAT SHE PULLED A MONICA.

452
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:49,438
SHE DOESN'T KNOW
WE SWITCHED IT.

453
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:53,734
AND THE NEXT TIME
YOU CATER FOR ME

454
00:19:53,734 --> 00:19:57,030
THERE'LL BE NOTHING
BUT ICE IN THE FREEZER.

455
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:59,406
THAT REALLY
MEANS A LOT.

456
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:01,241
OY, MOM,
DON'T BITE YOUR NAILS.

457
00:20:08,082 --> 00:20:09,167
HELLO.

458
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:10,710
HEY.
HEY.
HEY.

459
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:14,547
HELLO, CHANDLER.

460
00:20:14,547 --> 00:20:16,674
I LOVE YOU.

461
00:20:16,674 --> 00:20:18,425
HEY, WHAT'S GOING ON?

462
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:19,426
OH...

463
00:20:19,426 --> 00:20:20,803
( whispering )

464
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:24,849
NO, HE DOESN'T.

465
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:27,143
( laughing )

466
00:20:27,143 --> 00:20:30,396
TWO HOURS, THAT LASTED.

467
00:20:30,396 --> 00:20:32,314
SO DID YOU BREAK UP
WITH JOANNA?

468
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:33,774
I THINK SO.

469
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:35,193
IT'S A GOOD THING YOU GOT OUT
WHEN YOU DID

470
00:20:35,193 --> 00:20:39,238
BEFORE SHE BLEW UP
LIKE THAT VESUVIUS.

471
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:40,280
THE VOLCANO?

472
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:42,200
YEAH. AND SPEAKING OF VOLCANOES

473
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:46,829
MAN, ARE THEY A VIOLENT,
IGNEOUS ROCK FORMATION.

474
00:20:46,829 --> 00:20:48,122
WHAT?

475
00:20:48,122 --> 00:20:50,917
OH, YEAH-- LAVA SPEWING,
HOT ASH...

476
00:20:50,917 --> 00:20:53,711
OF COURSE, SOME ARE DORMANT.

477
00:20:53,711 --> 00:20:54,879
WHY ARE YOU TALKING
ABOUT VOLCANOES

478
00:20:54,879 --> 00:20:56,089
ALL OF A SUDDEN?

479
00:20:56,089 --> 00:20:57,840
WE CAN TALK
ABOUT SOMETHING ELSE.

480
00:20:57,840 --> 00:20:59,926
WHAT DO YOU WANT TO TALK ABOUT?
VIVISECTION?

481
00:20:59,926 --> 00:21:01,385
THE VAS...

482
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:03,470
DEFERENS?

483
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:05,848
THE VIETNAM WAR?

484
00:21:05,848 --> 00:21:07,892
OH, DID ANYBODY
SEE THAT DOCUMENTARY

485
00:21:07,892 --> 00:21:09,393
ON THE KOREAN WAR?

486
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:11,771
All:
OH, YEAH.

487
00:21:11,771 --> 00:21:13,564
KOREA IS SUCH
A BEAUTIFUL COUNTRY.

488
00:21:13,564 --> 00:21:15,441
WITH SUCH A SAD HISTORY.

489
00:21:15,441 --> 00:21:17,068
YEAH.

490
00:21:17,068 --> 00:21:18,360
COULD THERE BE MORE KIMS?

491
00:21:27,745 --> 00:21:28,829
Joanna:
WHO'S OUT THERE?

492
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:30,456
IT'S ME. GOOD MORNING.

493
00:21:30,456 --> 00:21:32,499
RACHEL, COULD YOU
COME IN HERE A MOMENT PLEASE?

494
00:21:32,499 --> 00:21:35,920
SURE. THEY DIDN'T
HAVE POPPY-SEED BAGELS

495
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:39,339
SO I... OH, MY WORD!

496
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:43,136
HI. I SEEM TO HAVE HAD
A SLIGHT OFFICE MISHAP.

497
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:45,805
COULD YOU PLEASE
GET THE KEY

498
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:47,306
OFF THE BACK
OF THE DOOR FOR ME?

499
00:21:47,306 --> 00:21:51,102
YEAH. OF COURSE. UM...

500
00:21:54,147 --> 00:21:55,397
I'M SO SORRY.

501
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:56,941
YOU CAN TELL
YOUR FRIEND CHANDLER

502
00:21:56,941 --> 00:21:59,735
THAT WE'RE DEFINITELY
BROKEN UP THIS TIME.

